  {"comment":"A level tray from a solid box 60 x 40 x 20: setback 5 at each 90 degree bend, so the base is 50 x 30. At a corner the two walls keep half the gap off the bisecting plane on their inner surfaces: each wall ends 2 + sqrt 2 short of the corner, its bend 5 + sqrt 2 short, where all the bend's material clears the plane. Walls (56 - 2 sqrt 2) and (36 - 2 sqrt 2) by 15, bends (50 - 2 sqrt 2) and (30 - 2 sqrt 2) long: developed 4260 - 120 sqrt 2 + 1.8 pi (160 - 8 sqrt 2); folded 2 (4260 - 120 sqrt 2) + 4 pi (160 - 8 sqrt 2)."},
