  {"comment":"An inclined tray: the profile (0,0) (60,6) (60,20) (0,20) extruded 40, its bottom rising 6 over 60 and its rim level. The end walls meet the base at 90 degrees plus and minus atan 0.1; the side walls are vertical, so their ends are not square to their inclined bends. Their bends end where they clear the corners' bisecting planes, the walls run on to those planes."},
